    "essentialQuestion": "How can transformations and key attributes be used to graph, analyze, and describe absolute value functions?",
    "teacherNotes": "Instructional sequence intentionally begins with general transformation language in an ALEKS-like graph-mapping progression, then narrows to absolute value. Reinforce the class rule “x’s lie; y’s tell the truth”: inside/x changes use opposite signs and reciprocal scale factors; outside/y changes act exactly as written. Require students to move defining points before connecting the transformed graph."
